@@ -0,0 +1,27 @@
+# conversation-focus-mode
+
+Renderer-only, session-scoped conversation focus mode. Public entry: `packages/ui/src/v4/focus-mode/contract.ts`. Layer: ui; requires shared and ui.
+
+## Intent
+
+`/force` in the local slash menu toggles focus rendering for the current session only. The renderer store keys the preference by stable workspace identity plus session id and persists real sessions to localStorage. Panes and windows of one session agree, other sessions remain isolated, and restarting restores the preference. Drafts and unknown workspaces are memory-only; storage failures fall back to memory. Nothing is written to settings, the host, a database, or provider traffic.
+
+Off renders the original `ConversationTimeline` with no focus computation. On renders only the latest two logical groups through the same timeline component; hidden rows never mount.
+
+## Invariants
+
+- A logical group closes only after `turnHeader.state === "completedSuccess"`; guided inputs never split a turn and assistant/tool completion does not close it.
+- Interrupted/failed/unknown fragments join the following continuation (or remain the trailing group) and never consume a two-group slot.
+- A leading `turnHeader` alone does not prove the group is complete: an interrupted prefix may belong to it. The first selected group needs one preceding success boundary or the true history start; loading stops there.
+- The latest window is recalculated from the current projection; expanded history uses all loaded rows without maintaining historical page anchors.
+- Latest-view completion has one bounded load owner, with an eight-request budget, no-progress stop and explicit retry. Expanding suspends it without resetting the budget; an in-flight result cannot initiate another focus load while expanded.
+- Only the enabled flag is persisted; restarting or reopening starts in the locked latest two-group phase. Latest is locked: wheel, touch and keyboard scroll only within the two selected groups and cannot page or unlock. Only the up button expands all already-loaded rows and delegates further pagination to the normal timeline; down and the host bottom action restore the locked latest window. `/force` remains enabled in both phases, with both controls always present.
+- `SessionPane` disables its legacy `shouldAutoLoadIncompleteLeadingTurn` effect while focus is enabled; latest completion and expanded normal pagination must not issue simultaneous loads.
+- Phase changes never remount the timeline or composer dock. Controls occupy a compact slot outside the scroll viewport and align horizontally with the visible composer input surface center, not the overall timeline center. Width, pane and status-panel layout changes update the alignment; if the input is unavailable or hidden, use the dock content center, then the slot center as a safe fallback. Observe sizes only on the slot and the input/dock target; watch only the dock's class/style attributes for individual translate changes that do not resize or transition. Clean up observers and transition animation callbacks on unmount, and do not alter scrolling. The status panel is offset below that slot while focus is enabled, including in narrow panes; it returns to its original position when disabled.
+- Pending guides and runtime retry remain live. The turn navigator follows normal admission on loaded rows when expanded, without triggering its bulk history hydration, and is hidden in the latest window.
+
+## Integration points
+
+- `SessionPane` reads `useSessionFocusMode(scopeKey)`, passes `{ enabled, toggle }` into the compat slash builder, chooses the wrapper component, and guards its legacy auto-load effect.
+- `slash-commands/commands/focus-mode.ts` builds `/force`; the existing integration boundary still filters exact `cliSlashCommandNames` collisions. The command is a pure view toggle and remains available when write actions are denied.
+- `ConversationTimeline` gains one optional `navigationAdapter` (scroll element, back-to-bottom override, forced bottom button, window placement). Without it, behavior is unchanged.
